        "observed": "Older2007 streetside context: short broad metal dome/cross on square brick drum; ochre church walls and low red tile roofs. A separate west courtyard gateway with large center and two small arched openings stands ahead of the church; trees obscure the main lower facade. Context image, not a source for exact threshold or current roof state."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_Sophia_Church,_Thessaloniki_(east_side).jpg",
        "image": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7c/Saint_Sophia_Church%2C_Thessaloniki_%28east_side%29.jpg",
        "observed": "2018 east side: exposed warm brick and pale masonry; broad projecting central polygonal apse with paired/large arched glazing and hip tile roof, smaller side apses/ranges with low red tile caps. Square clerestory drum has large dark arched windows and low round metal dome/cross above. Northwest small square bell tower has arched upper openings and short tile hip roof. Church courtyard sits behind a retaining wall/metal fence; exact ground/thresholds not established."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Αγία_Σοφία,_Θεσσαλονίκη_3859.jpg",
        "image": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/%CE%91%CE%B3%CE%AF%CE%B1_%CE%A3%CE%BF%CF%86%CE%AF%CE%B1%2C_%CE%98%CE%B5%CF%83%CF%83%CE%B1%CE%BB%CE%BF%CE%BD%CE%AF%CE%BA%CE%B7_3859.jpg",
        "observed": "2019 clear west facade: ochre upper plaster over pale warm masonry lower band, one horizontal row of about ten narrow arched clerestory windows, three wood doors and four larger dark arched lower glazed/grille fields. Central entry has a broad stepped carved round masonry arch/pale jambs. Brick square drum has three arched front windows; short round terracotta upper band supports low ribbed gray-green metal dome and cross. Small northwest brick bell tower has paired arched openings and low dark tile hip cap. No fresco/interior or carved iconography geometry inferred."
      }
    ]
